<section class="text-level-3">
  <h2 data-toc-label="Manage environment variables" class="mt-0 text-size-heading-3">
    Verify several environments
  </h2>
    
    <ul>
      <li>
        Define the variables that change depending on the environment in a <code>.env</code> file
        <pre><code class="properties">
          # .env.preprod
          BASE_URL=https://my-app.preprod/
          ADMIN_LOGIN=superuser@example.com
          ADMIN_PASSWD=testing
        </code></pre>

      </li>

       <li class="mt-200">
        <p>Use env variables in test scripts</p>

        <pre><code class="python">
          page.get_by_role("textbox", name="Mot de passe *").fill(
            os.getenv("ADMIN_PASSWD")
          )
        </code></pre>

      </li>

      <li class="mt-200">
        <p>Define the <code>.env</code> file to use for the test session</p>
        <pre><code class="sh">
          uv run pytest --env-file .env.preprod  # this overrides the env-file defined in pytest.ini
        </code></pre>
      </li>
    </ul>
</section>